    "I read your user settings at `/tmp/p2b-f6TSgw/home/.claude/settings.json`. It has two problems, though the error only reported one:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"model\": \"no-such-model-p2b\",\n  \"permissions\": {\n    \"defaultMode\": \"bogus\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**1. `permissions.defaultMode` is `\"bogus\"`, which isn't a valid mode.**\n\nThe suggested fix describes some of the modes wrong, so here's what each one actually does:\n- `\"default\"`: asks for permission the usual way.\n- `\"acceptEdits\"`: approves file edits automatically. The suggestion said it \"asks before file changes,\" which is backwards.\n- `\"plan\"`: Claude only reads and plans, and makes no changes.\n- `\"auto\"` / `\"dontAsk\"`: fewer prompts, with different handling for tool calls that haven't been pre-approved.\n- `\"bypassPermissions\"`: approves every tool call without asking. I wouldn't pick this one just to clear the error.\n\n**My recommendation:** set it to `\"default\"`. That fixes the error without giving any tool more access.\n\n**2. `model` is `\"no-such-model-p2b\"`, which isn't a real model ID.** It wasn't in the error you pasted, but Claude Code will probably fail or fall back when it tries to use it. I suggest deleting the line so Claude Code uses its built-in default model. If you want a specific model, I can set something like `\"claude-opus-5-5\"` or `\"claude-sonnet-5-5\"` instead.\n\nBoth fixes edit your global user settings, so I'll wait for your go-ahead. The change I'd make:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"permissions\": {\n    \"defaultMode\": \"default\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nShould I apply both fixes? Or tell me if you'd prefer a different mode, or a specific model instead of deleting the `model` line."
